      "Reversing object alpha order produced zero changes for coverage but did not prove acceptable readability. That former assertion is not final acceptance evidence."
    ]
  },
  "limits": [
    "A newly encountered solid obstruction can temporarily cover the target during a gesture because membership is held. In the four-hole full-circle run the 180-degree moving view is obscured; the stopped rear view automatically fades that obstruction and clearly shows all four marked holes.",
    "Alpha blending and whole-source center sorting approximate intersecting translucent shells; this work does not claim physically exact order-independent transparency. Actual before/rear/side and full-circle views were inspected.",
    "Raw source lip contours, tessellation facets and pre-existing source contact irregularities remain. No source vertices, topology, triangle IDs or placements were modified."
